Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:53:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 191/209] feat(area): trigger bounds component

A second consumer of the shape contract, deliberately small, and the proof
that the contract is not secretly the Area component's private interface: it
needs no engine change at all and never touches a CArea.

"Trigger Bounds" takes the local AABB of whatever shape sits on the same
entity and feeds it to the stock IEntityTriggerComponent, followed by
InvalidateTrigger() so that entities already standing inside are caught rather
than waiting for the next crossing. It binds by the same rule the Area
component uses, listens for the same shape change notification, and creates
its trigger flagged NoSave for the same reason - the box is derived from the
shape, so it must not be written to the level a second time.

It is a proximity trigger, not an area: CProximityTriggerSystem puts the
triggering entity in nParam[1] where CArea puts its area id, so an entity
should carry either this or the Area component, not both. That is a documented
sharp edge of the engine, written down in the header rather than papered over.

No per-frame work: the trigger follows the entity by itself, so the component
only subscribes to property and reset events.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
